CONTEXT Migration INCLUDES Garden FROM "../layout/garden.adl" AS old
CONTEXT Migration IN ENGLISH
-- An atom of a relation is an atom of its concepts. The migration context has a relation of its own
-- on old.Gardener, such as a register of copying, and Bob is only in that relation.
-- The existing system has no table for Gardener, so the atoms of old.Gardener are read from the columns
-- of every relation that holds them: Ann from old.keeper, Bob from mentor (claim PRF-27).
-- The interface makes old.Gardener a concept of objects, which must not give it a table in the
-- database of the existing system. ampersand validate compares the SQL of I[old.Gardener] with the evaluator.

RELATION mentor[old.Gardener*old.Gardener]
POPULATION mentor CONTAINS [ ("Bob", "Bob") ]

INTERFACE Gardeners : I[old.Gardener] cRud BOX [ mentor : mentor cRud ]

ENDCONTEXT
